# Normed Presumed Chemistry (NPC)

version: 1
range: 0..24

# Evidence classes
observation: direct or explicitly supplied experimental observation
measurement: quantified observation with units/provenance
structure: candidate atom/molecule/material structure
bond: bond existence or compatibility hypothesis
valence: valence and charge-balance constraint
geometry: spatial/structural compatibility
electronic_state: electronic and polarity compatibility
reaction_relationship: reaction/kinetic relationship
compound_family_similarity: similarity to established chemical families
thermodynamic_consequence: derived energy/equilibrium consequence
astronomical_context: periodic, planetary, stellar, or cosmic context

# Ratio norms
ratio: numerator / denominator, with undefined ratios retained as uncertain
similarity: bounded relational score, not identity
signal: experimental or observational support for a candidate
bond_ratio: relative compatibility among candidate bonds
valence_ratio: relative compatibility with expected valence
symmetry_ratio: agreement among independent structural relations

# Causal symmetry ordering
order:
  1 observation
  2 measurement
  3 structure
  4 bond
  5 valence
  6 geometry
  7 electronic_state
  8 reaction_relationship
  9 compound_family_similarity
  10 thermodynamic_consequence
  11 astronomical_context

# 0..24 inference interpretation
level 0: raw subject; no useful evidence
level 1..4: direct observations dominate
level 5..8: elementary structural inference
level 9..12: valence and bonding inference
level 13..16: similarity and compound-family inference
level 17..20: multi-property convergent inference
level 21..23: strong convergent model support
level 24: maximum model-supported inference; never experimental proof

# Stochastic rule
stochastic_evaluation: deterministic seeded perturbation may rank competing hypotheses
stochastic_limit: perturbation cannot manufacture evidence or erase contradictory observation

# Epistemic rule
observed != derived != inferred
inferred_property requires supporting ratios and explicit uncertainty
high_score != scientific_certainty
